<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Worcester</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1218</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worcester">Worcester</a> was the agreement of 1218 by which the minority government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a> recognised the dominance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-the-great">Llywelyn the Great</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. Llywelyn did homage to the young king and was allowed to keep the castles and lands he had taken, including custody of royal lordships in the south, confirming him as the leading ruler in Wales.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-worcester.jpg" alt="Treaty of Worcester" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tipcake · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pen_Llywelyn_ab_Iorwerth,_Castell_Degannwy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
